// Title: Hiding Files with Attrib.exe
// Sigma ID: 4281cb20-2994-4580-aa63-c8b86d019934
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Sami Ruohonen
// Date: 2019-01-16 | Modified: 2023-03-14
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1564.001
// Description: Detects usage of attrib.exe to hide files from users.
// False positives:
//   - IgfxCUIService.exe hiding *.cui files via .bat script (attrib.exe a child of cmd.exe and igfxCUIService.exe is the parent of the cmd.exe)
//   - Msiexec.exe hiding desktop.ini
// References:
//   - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/unit42-sure-ill-take-new-combojack-malware-alters-clipboards-steal-cryptocurrency/
//   - https://www.uptycs.com/blog/lolbins-are-no-laughing-matter
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_attrib_hiding_files.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 2 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\attrib.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "ATTRIB.EXE") and ProcessCommandLine contains " +h ") and (not(ProcessCommandLine contains "\\desktop.ini ")) and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" and ProcessCommandLine matches regex @"(?i)^\+R \+H \+S \+A \\.*\.cui$" and InitiatingProcessCommandLine matches regex @"(?i)^C:\\WINDOWS\\system32\\.*\.bat$")))
